{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1463907-obtenebration-thought-experiment-v20","id":1463907,"title":"Obtenebration Thought Experiment V20","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-10-14T16:46:02-07:00","id":1463907,"title":"Obtenebration Thought Experiment V20","content":"So, I was making a character for a V20 game, and I had settled on a Lasombra. I wanted to play around with Abyss Mysticism, because it seemed neat. And I had a thought that was a bit of a potential game-breaker, but it was a sufficiently interesting idea that I felt like posting it and seeing what people thought.<br /> <br /> This concept relies on a few different things.<br /> <br /> 1.) Obtenebration 3, Occult 3, and the Abyss Mysticism Ritual 'Feed the Darkness' at bare minimum.<br /> 2.) Dominate 4 makes it significantly more convenient to keep your inmate population under control.<br /> <br /> The concept is kind of a simple one, the idea is a prison. To make it work the vampire who wants to pull this off will need to construct a secret prison, or at least a prison that isn't well observed. The idea I had was basically a circular chamber beneath the vampires haven, there they keep mortal prisoners in the dark.<br /> <br /> Then, since so far as I could find there is no durational limit on the use, you put an Obtenebration 3 'Arm of the Abyss' in a hole in the ceiling of each cell. This relies on the interpretation that A.) You can create multiple 'batches' of arms using successive actions. and B.) That the arms do not simply expire on their own.<br /> <br /> Each night on waking, the Abyss Mystic enacts the ritual 'Feed the Darkness' this ritual allows them to feed remotely, using their controlled arms of the Abyss. From there, whenever they need blood, they reach out to the pit they've established beneath their haven, and the arms there that are in contact with the prisoners feed, sending the blood points on to the controlling vampire and topping off their vitae. With something around 53 'Residents' you can easily top off your blood pool from 0 every day as an 8th gen without risking permanent harm. Which you probably won't need.<br /> <br /> (Right around this was where I realized I was scheming up a lightless hell prison to replace the inconvenience and humanity loss risk of hunting which kind of defeated the point.)<br /> <br /> But, while a potent setup it's not without it's complications.<br /> <br /> Firstly, Setup. Maintaining a secret prison isn't easy. Particularly if you want to keep your donors healthy. Not only do you need to build a prison in absolute secrecy, you also need to staff it with caretakers to feed and maintain the prisoners health, guards to stop intruders or escape attempts. And you're gonna have to keep <b>all</b> of that hidden or at least disguised somehow. Whether it's as a mental hospital, or something else, you'll have to find some explanation for the steady stream of medical supplies and food provided. Why people keep disappearing into it and why there's noone coming out. Also you'll preferably have to do so without the local kindred community finding out, because otherwise you lose the surprise factor of being able to simple refill your blood pool on the fly.<br /> <br /> Secondly, The Kiss is a distraction. Just because you're feeding remotely doesn't mean you aren't feeding. So unless you can make the roll to prevent getting lost in the feeding, you can't do this in combat, and even if you can there's always the chance you roll poorly and leave yourself wide open.<br /> <br /> Thirdly, As touched on before, other Kindred who don't want to deal with someone who can refresh their blood pool constantly will try to destroy or coopt the place. Elders in particular might not enjoy a younger vampire having a setup that might help them fight on more even terms.<br /> <br /> Anyhow, thoughts? Issues?<br /> <br /> Honestly, while not necessarily something I would want to see a player doing, I Could see it being a neat mechanic for a 'boss' battle that isn't just another Methuselah or an interesting plot, You have to find the Prince/Archbishops hell-pit prisons scattered all over the city and burn them if you want to be able to have a chance at overthrowing them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-15T06:13:23-07:00","id":1464019,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure what the rules say exactly, but other than a (merit?, combo discipline?) keeping a construct in sunlight going for an hour, my general rule is dawn ends shadow construct light or no. This could be very wrong, feel free to point out the error of my ways.<br /> <br /> I've never had a player spending exp to actually get Dominate 4. Maybe we just don't see it right, I guess a bunch of docile blood bags is nice if you don't mind feeding them. If you take the long effort to condition 50 some people, I see no need for cells. Live on a farm and let them grow their own food I guess.<br /> <br /> As far as saving you humanity rolls I agree, your toon went dark and has a really low humanity after turning 50 some people into mentally crippled slaves locked in a cell until they die of poor health from lack of exercise and vitamin d lol.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-15T07:58:11-07:00","id":1464031,"title":"","content":"Run your idea straight, <b>make a prison</b>. If it is in the US, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_United_States_state_correction_agencies\" target=\"_blank\">here is a list to help you</a>. Chose the state correction facility for your setting and you'll see a list of prisons that includes number of inmates.<br /> <br /> Most US correction facilities are private, and the system have terrible oversight even in real life, it have a strong lobby and offer one of the worse prison systems in the world in terms of human rights. Your character will have their herd and be paid for it, sometimes a guaranteed income equivalent to at least 90% of capacity even if working below it. That's IRL, in WoD it may be worse.<br /> <br /> You won't need to deprive them of anything they wouldn't be deprived anyway. No one cares about them and you don't feed during day, so they don't need to stay in your dark tentacles all the time. Actually, given that you'll take care of their health for feeding purposes, you'll run one of the most humane facilities in the country, even if you're a complete jerk. And it's not as if they were be free if they weren't under your claws.<br /> <br /> The only thing I'll point out is that you actually do need more inmates to avoid permanent harm. It is not only about the time to recover lost blood, 1 pint worth of blood of our iron reserves takes from 4 weeks to 2 months to replenish, if you consume too fast they'll recover blood but develop anemia, so you're better with 60 people for each BP you want per day.<br /> <br /> Luckily you'll see that prisons with more than a thousand inmates aren't uncommon, and with good healthcare and a reinforced iron diet you can reduce to 30 people, so 900 inmates gives you a safe supply of 30 BP/day. They may have some health problems here and there, but people die or disappear in the prison system with some regularity anyway, and you have new inmates to replenish your stocks.<br /> <br /> IRL this situation is slowly changing since 2009, although incredibly inhumane to date. But this is WoD, so it can be still just as bad as it used to be when more than 7 in 1 thousand Americans were incarcerated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}